cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lumina: a declarative animation engine"
message: "If you use Lumina in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hashim
    given-names: Sakar
    alias: SakarZaidan
repository-code: "https://github.com/SakarZaidan/lumina"
url: "https://sakarzaidan.github.io/lumina/"
abstract: >-
  Lumina is a declarative animation engine written in Rust. A scene is a
  JSON document (the Lumina Scene Format) describing objects and a timeline
  of keyframes; the engine evaluates that timeline at any point in time and
  rasterises the result deterministically on a CPU backend (tiny-skia), a
  GPU-capable backend (vello/wgpu), or in WebAssembly. The format is
  schema-validated so that scenes can be generated and repaired
  programmatically, including by language models.
keywords:
  - animation
  - rendering
  - rust
  - declarative
  - webassembly
  - data-visualization
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
